Z||000025||Slammed Fiero||12-17-2000||02:14 PM||||Canadian Spec motors never had more HP. The only thing that MIGHT have been changed is the exhaust. There are canadian and US spec exhaust systems for corvettes , there part #'s are designated by "For export only" The allante had a better intake manifold which Team python runs on their car. But I believe that only increased power by 10 to 15hp.<P><BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>Worked for GM head office in marketing and a GM dealer for a while , ordered a few corvette exhaust systems......||||reg||1
Z||000026||rockcrawl||12-17-2000||09:05 PM||||The Canadian and US engines both had 9.5:1 compression. I'd still rather have a 135hp V8 than a 135hp V6. But is it worth the work to do the swap, especially with the 4.1's reliability problems? Maybe. I have a 4.1 Goodwrench motor with over 200,000 miles on it, still runs strong.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||jlruiz67||12-17-2000||11:22 PM||||I have already email you and I hope you can find the time to send the information.<BR>jlruiz2k@hotmail.com<P>please no spam||||reg||1
Z||000028||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||12-18-2000||12:19 AM||||From the pictures, this looks like  a tight squeeze getting the Caddy V8 into a Fiero.<P>Did you have room for the recall madated splash shields.  It seem like if you have leak, something hot is likely to be nearby.<P>Does the engine ever strike the firewall or trunk?  It looks like it does not have room to move under torque.  I bet that Caddy V8 has lots more torque than a 2.8 V6.<P>I also bet the power is smooth and plentiful.  There's no doubt that the car will be a joy on the freeway.  The question is will you be able to keep it under the speed of sound.<P>Have fun, but consider the possibility of leaks.  Plastic bodied cars have been known to burn very quickly.  <P>I always here that the V8 conversions are so powerful that the owner is afraid to push the car.  Has anyone had problems with a V8 in a Fiero?||||reg||1
